  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n**What changed.** Test-only. `stepped_stock_rapid::a_coarse_stock_whose_source_is_gone_is_never_acquitted` was red on main: the post was still blocked, but by the coarse-import refusal instead of the rapid law.\n\n**Root cause.** The refusal order did not change. The post gate (`posting::verification_report_by`) has run the fidelity clause (#864) first all along, and since #1056 point 3 a fidelity refusal silences the sim's lines. What changed is the fixture's input. PR #1127 (#1056 point 1) made a `FromModel` stock carry its source's chord. Before it, the coarse casting lost its 2.5 mm chord once it was deleted, so only the rapid law blocked. Now the stock keeps the chord and the fidelity clause refuses the post by the casting's name. That is the earlier and safer refusal, so the test is updated and the gate is not changed. The decision is in `docs/decisions/1336-coarse-refusal-first.md`.\n\n**The test now pins**, for both the part-sourced and the stock-sourced Bore:\n- the coarse, deleted casting's post is blocked by the coarse-import refusal, matched by name (`model 'casting'` and `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE`);\n- the rapid law still convicts that dive (`Warning::RapidInStock` on the op), so the stock-top acquittal is still refused on an unknown chord;\n- the same program with the exact casting deleted, where no fidelity refusal comes first, is blocked by the rapid law by name (`rapid move <at> `).\n\n**How tested.** `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (app:stepped_stock_rapid, 8/8). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test stepped_stock_rapid -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n**Not exercised.** No product code changed, so no other suites were run.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1336\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
